00:05:15.286 --> 00:05:16.176
calories.

00:05:16.176 --> 00:05:17.686
Also commonly reported,

00:05:17.686 --> 00:05:19.836
consistently high energy
levels, better sleep,

00:05:19.836 --> 00:05:23.016
improved focus, mental
clarity, and a return

00:05:23.016 --> 00:05:24.636
to a healthy digestive system,

00:05:24.636 --> 00:05:27.496
improved athletic performance,
and a sunnier disposition.

00:05:27.496 --> 00:05:30.406
I know way doubt that there
were these benefits in

00:05:30.406 --> 00:05:32.126
some of the people that have done Whole30.

00:05:32.126 --> 00:05:34.106
To make this promise
that this is gonna happen

00:05:34.106 --> 00:05:35.796
to almost everybody that does it,

00:05:35.796 --> 00:05:38.456
I don't like over-promising
results to my patients

00:05:38.456 --> 00:05:41.186
because I think that ultimately
provides them a disservice.

00:05:41.186 --> 00:05:43.856
It makes them believe that
this is the miracle cure-all

00:05:43.856 --> 00:05:45.396
thing that they've been waiting for,

00:05:45.396 --> 00:05:46.229
and in some cases it is,

00:05:46.229 --> 00:05:47.469
it may be true.

00:05:47.469 --> 00:05:50.046
Someone who has been eating
junk food their whole life,

00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:52.636
has disordered digestive
system because they've

00:05:52.636 --> 00:05:53.490
been eating this junk,

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.176
this can help and this
can change their life,

00:05:56.176 --> 00:05:58.754
but to make it seem like
no matter who you are

00:05:58.754 --> 00:06:00.136
this is gonna change your life,

00:06:00.136 --> 00:06:01.606
I think it's a bit of an over-statement.

00:06:01.606 --> 00:06:03.876
As a practicing physician,
I know that patients

00:06:03.876 --> 00:06:05.119
who are suffering with diseases are

00:06:05.119 --> 00:06:08.545
really susceptible to any
kind of marketing hype

00:06:08.545 --> 00:06:11.266
that's promising them a
cure for their illness's.

00:06:11.266 --> 00:06:12.750
On the cover of this book it says,

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.456
more significant, many people
have reported the magical

00:06:16.456 --> 00:06:19.626
elimination of a variety
of symptoms, diseases, and

00:06:19.626 --> 00:06:21.656
conditions in just 30 days,

00:06:21.656 --> 00:06:23.910
and they go onto list a
whole host of conditions

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:27.032
including eczema, psoriasis,
chronic fatigue, asthma,

00:06:27.032 --> 00:06:30.224
sinus infections, allergies,
migraines, acid reflex,

00:06:30.224 --> 00:06:34.041
Crohn's, celiac, IBS,
bipolar disorder, depression,

00:06:34.041 --> 00:06:38.826
Lyme's disease, endometriosis,
PCOS, and even autism.

00:06:38.826 --> 00:06:41.276
They don't out right
state that Whole30 is the

00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:42.956
cure for any of these conditions because

00:06:42.956 --> 00:06:44.166
then they would be in legal trouble,

00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:46.966
but the fact that they're even
conflating the possibility

00:06:46.966 --> 00:06:50.484
that Whole30 can be a
treatment for autism or a cure

00:06:50.484 --> 00:06:51.736
for autism,

00:06:51.736 --> 00:06:54.006
I think that borderline is
a little bit ridiculous and

00:06:54.006 --> 00:06:56.086
again is doing a
disservice to our patients.

00:06:56.086 --> 00:06:57.886
What I think is quite
interesting is that some of

00:06:57.886 --> 00:07:01.479
the symptoms that Whole30 aims to remove,

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:05.256
can actually be caused by
a nutritional deficiency,

00:07:05.256 --> 00:07:07.370
and Whole30 on its own
can exacerbate some of

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.176
these nutritional deficiencies.

00:07:09.176 --> 00:07:10.642
For example, imagine
I have a patient who's

00:07:10.642 --> 00:07:13.706
chronically fatigued and
having difficulty with

00:07:13.706 --> 00:07:16.296
energy levels and sleep so on so fourth,

00:07:16.296 --> 00:07:18.849
and I find that there Vitamin D deficient,

00:07:18.849 --> 00:07:21.446
that they have a very low Vitamin D level.

00:07:21.446 --> 00:07:24.486
Now, eliminating all types
of dairy will certainly

00:07:25.469 --> 00:07:26.302
exacerbate that condition,

00:07:26.302 --> 00:07:28.646
but had I not run these
tests beforehand and the

00:07:28.646 --> 00:07:31.216
patient went on Whole30
without consulting me first,

00:07:31.216 --> 00:07:33.186
think about the negative outcomes
that could have occurred.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:35.519
Putting junk and processed
foods aside for a moment,

00:07:35.519 --> 00:07:38.037
the foods that you're
eliminating while on Whole30,

00:07:38.037 --> 00:07:40.054
can be problematic to some people,

00:07:40.054 --> 00:07:43.432
but for most, eliminating
them will yield no benefit

00:07:43.432 --> 00:07:45.790
and in actually some
cases can fuel nutritional

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.106
deficiencies or even
exacerbate medical problems.

00:07:49.106 --> 00:07:51.436
Something else that's
problematic is that Whole30

00:07:51.436 --> 00:07:54.181
tries very hard to be a
proper elimination diet,

00:07:54.181 --> 00:07:56.700
which is the gold standard
that doctors use trying

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.406
to identify food sensitivities,

00:07:59.406 --> 00:08:00.496
but while it comes close,

00:08:00.496 --> 00:08:02.366
it's not exactly accurate.

00:08:02.366 --> 00:08:04.246
For example, if were gonna
do a restrictive diet

00:08:04.246 --> 00:08:05.079
of any sort,

00:08:05.079 --> 00:08:07.136
we would do it for 90 days because that's

00:08:07.136 --> 00:08:08.923
how long it takes for the
immune system to sort of

00:08:08.923 --> 00:08:10.676
shut down its response.

00:08:10.676 --> 00:08:12.841
On top of that, I rarely jump to saying

00:08:12.841 --> 00:08:15.696
let's eliminate everything
and see what sticks.

00:08:15.696 --> 00:08:18.156
It's kind of a shock on
approach that may work in

00:08:18.156 --> 00:08:20.395
some instances, but may
also make my patient's

00:08:20.395 --> 00:08:23.456
life so much more problematic
than it needs to be,

00:08:23.456 --> 00:08:25.638
and in their reintroduction
protocol within the book,

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:28.764
they say to introduce foods
every two, three days,

00:08:28.764 --> 00:08:30.960
but then they go on to say
to contradict themselves,

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.096
that you may have a negative
reaction a week later.

00:08:34.096 --> 00:08:36.886
So, at that point you've
already introduced three foods.

00:08:36.886 --> 00:08:39.146
How do you know which one is
causing a negative reaction?

00:08:39.146 --> 00:08:41.706
It really becomes problematic
that this is not done

00:08:41.706 --> 00:08:44.636
in a systemic way like we
would do in a medical center,

00:08:44.636 --> 00:08:47.926
and finally I'm not a huge
fan of restrictive diets

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:50.656
like this because generally
you they don't have long-term

00:08:50.656 --> 00:08:54.336
success rates and I fear that
there could be psychological

00:08:54.336 --> 00:08:56.366
problems that develop
when you say to yourself,

00:08:56.366 --> 00:08:59.044
you absolutely can't have a
single cookie or your a failure.

00:08:59.044 --> 00:09:01.837
I mean, that sort of anxiety
is not good for anybody,

00:09:01.837 --> 00:09:04.439
especially those who are
prone to disordered eating.

00:09:07.676 --> 00:09:12.136
So, what's my overall take
on this Whole30 challenge?

00:09:12.136 --> 00:09:13.346
I think it's quite interesting.

00:09:13.346 --> 00:09:15.756
I think it's cool to be
able to give yourself a

00:09:15.756 --> 00:09:17.676
test of will power for thirty days.

00:09:17.676 --> 00:09:20.332
I am the main proponent
of removing junk food,

00:09:20.332 --> 00:09:23.548
processed food, increasing
whole foods in your diet, so

00:09:23.548 --> 00:09:25.816
I totally agree with Whole30 on that.

00:09:25.816 --> 00:09:28.756
However, if I have a patient
that's having some sort of

00:09:28.756 --> 00:09:30.080
symptoms that their concerned about,

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.256
I wouldn't jump to giving
them a restrictive diet

00:09:33.256 --> 00:09:35.096
to figure out if it's the result of food

00:09:35.096 --> 00:09:37.646
sensitivities without
doing some testing first.

00:09:37.646 --> 00:09:38.746
So my recommendation,

00:09:38.746 --> 00:09:41.107
if your having some sort
of weird symptoms going on

00:09:41.107 --> 00:09:42.803
and you're considering Whole30,

00:09:42.803 --> 00:09:44.126
pump the brakes a little bit.

00:09:44.126 --> 00:09:46.983
Ask your doctor, talked
to a registered dietician,

00:09:46.983 --> 00:09:48.349
is this right for you, have you checked

00:09:48.349 --> 00:09:50.197
everything else that
can be contributing to

00:09:50.197 --> 00:09:51.516
your symptoms?

00:09:51.516 --> 00:09:53.416
Once you do that and you
have the all clear from

00:09:53.416 --> 00:09:54.623
a registered health professional,

00:09:54.623 --> 00:09:57.186
by all means check it out
and let me know how it goes.

00:09:57.186 --> 00:09:59.676
Whole30 isn't for everybody
and it's not perfect,

00:09:59.676 --> 00:10:02.016
but there's some certain
core principles within

00:10:02.016 --> 00:10:05.486
Whole30 that are absolutely
ideal for everybody,

00:10:05.486 --> 00:10:08.266
and I think by following it,
learning a little bit more

00:10:08.266 --> 00:10:09.145
about our own bodies,

00:10:09.145 --> 00:10:11.066
that can actually do some good,

